                "text": "I'm tracing the path: it starts at row0 col7 heading down, but hits an obstacle at row2 col7, so it detours left around the obstacle block before continuing downward, based on how the 2s shift columns across rows3-4.\n\nThen continuing down, another obstacle appears further down, and the path seems to shift into a new column permanently rather than returning, unlike the first detour. I'm puzzling over why the two obstacle types behave differently -- one returns to the original column, one doesn't -- and considering that maybe the numeric label of the obstacle determines whether the path bypasses and returns or bypasses and stays deflected.\n\nSomething's inconsistent between the two obstacle cases, so maybe the 1-bars are blocking the path and forcing a redirect rather than a simple outline trace. I'm reconsidering: perhaps when the path hits a 3-bar, it checks the cell below for a 1, and if blocked, it reroutes around the bar differently than I assumed.\n\nTracing further down col9 through rows 9-11, then hitting a 3-bar at row13 that forces a jump left to col6. Testing a pattern: it seems 3-bars always divert left while 1-bars divert right, which holds consistently across all the cases checked so far.",
